  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "The design exposes an untrusted ticket source to shared-service-account identity operations. The MFA reset path is reduced from critical to high only by a raw-action approval gate, but that gate runs at high volume and does not bind requester identity to the account owner. The more severe present issue is the direct delivery of a temporary pass to the ticket opener with no structural recipient binding, leaving residual risk at critical today. Forecast remains critical because removing or weakening analyst approval reopens the reset path fully, while the pass-delivery path already lacks an effective structural control. Manual validation was applied against the checklist because scripts could not be run."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration in the provided artifacts, not observed runtime behavior.",
